**$V_t$** — node equation at a (open circuit): $\frac{v_a - V_s}{R_1} + \frac{v_a}{R_2} = I_s$, so
$v_{oc} = \left(\frac{V_s}{R_1} + I_s\right)(R_1 \parallel R_2)$ = ({{Vs/R1|A}} + {{Is|A}}) × {{Rt|Ω}} = {{Voc|V}}
**$R_t$** — short $V_s$, open $I_s$: $R_t = R_1 \parallel R_2$ = {{Rt|Ω}}
So $V_t$ = **{{Voc|V}}**. (By superposition: $V_s$ alone gives {{Vs*R2/(R1 + R2)|V}}, $I_s$ alone gives {{Is*Rt|V}}.)

